FP8 attention K/V caches for Flash Next on the native CUDA engine (the engine keeps bf16 there): each position and KV head is E4M3 codes with an fp32 scale (amax/448, as the other families' kv_fp8.cuh), 528 bytes a position for keys or values instead of 1024. A stream's 262,144-token window takes ~4.7 GiB instead of 8.1 GiB. The indexer keys, pooled keys and everything else stay bf16. The writer quantizes after the key norm and rope; the readers cp.async the codes into a staging area, convert to bf16 (code x scale, rounded once) and feed the unchanged mma tiles, so each row's result still depends on that row only (greedy replies are byte-identical with drafts on and off). Switch: wt.kv_fp8 in cuda_prompt_wt.zig and KV8 in flashnext_pages.cuh (compile time; both false = the bf16 caches).

